sequenceDiagram
    participant Tester as [Person]<br> Tester User
    participant Generator as [System=TCMS CLI - Quality: Alpha]<br>Test Case Generator
    participant Editor as [Program=$Editor - Quality: Mature]<br>Manual Editor
    participant Generate as [Program=Bash - Quality: Beta]<br> test-executor generate
    participant Bash as [Program=Bash - Quality: Mature]<br> Bash
    participant DUT as [System/Program=DUT - Quality: Under Inspection]<br>Device Under Test
    participant Verifier as [System=TCMS CLI - Quality: Alpha]<br>Test Verifier
    participant Reports as [System=TCMS Reports - Quality: Beta]<br>Documentation Generator
    participant Plan as VV Plan (plans/)
    participant Exec as VV Exec (test-executor execute)
    participant Verif as VV Verifier (verifier)
    participant RunRec as VV Test run record (runs/)
    participant Matrix as VV Trace matrix (test-executor trace-matrix)
    participant Report as VV Report (test-executor report)

    Note over Tester,Report: All paths in the V&V section are relative to the scenario folder that the acceptance driver creates, not the repo root. plans/, runs/ and requirements/ sit under that folder.

    Tester ->> Generator: generate
    Tester ->> Editor: generate
    Note over Editor,Tester: Produces Artifact: Test Case (YAML)<br>PK={id}

    Tester ->> Generate: Create Test Case Shell Script (input: Test Case YAML)
    Note over Generate,Tester: Artifact: Test Case Shell Script (.sh)

    %% V&V path: plan -> execute -> verify -> test-run record -> trace matrix -> report (IDs A1..A7, S1..S6)
    %% vv-arrow A1
    Tester ->> Plan: validate test plan (no file written, stdout only)
    Note over Plan,Tester: A1 example: validate-yaml plans/TC-REQ001-NR.yaml
    Note over Plan: S1 reads: plans/ writes: nothing

    %% vv-arrow A2
    Plan ->> Exec: execute test case plan
    Note over Plan,Exec: A2 example: test-executor execute plans/TC-REQ001-NR.yaml
    Note over Exec: S2 reads: plans/ writes: runs/logs/ (location to be confirmed)

    %% vv-arrow A3
    Exec ->> Verif: verify execution logs against plans (no test-run record)
    Note over Exec,Verif: A3 example: verifier -f runs/logs -d plans -F yaml -o reports/verification/verification.yaml --run-id RUN-FAKE-001 --build-id FAKE-BUILD-1 --tester fake-tester --environment 'fake environment' --no-test-run
    Note over Verif: S3 reads: runs/logs/, plans/ writes: reports/verification/

    %% vv-arrow A4
    Verif ->> RunRec: write test run record
    Note over Verif,RunRec: A4 example: verifier -f runs/logs -d plans -F yaml -o reports/verification/verification.yaml --run-id RUN-FAKE-001 --build-id FAKE-BUILD-1 --tester fake-tester --environment 'fake environment' --test-run runs/RUN-FAKE-001.yml
    Note over RunRec: S4 reads: runs/logs/, plans/ writes: runs/

    %% vv-arrow A5
    RunRec ->> Matrix: build trace matrix from requirements and runs
    Note over RunRec,Matrix: A5 example: test-executor trace-matrix plans --requirements requirements/requirements.txt --runs runs --id TM-FAKE-001 --baseline-id BL-FAKE-001 -o reports/matrix/trace_matrix.yaml --no-coverage-check
    Note over Matrix: S5 reads: requirements/, plans/, runs/ writes: reports/matrix/

    %% vv-arrow A6
    Matrix ->> Report: render traceability report (Markdown)
    Note over Matrix,Report: A6 example: test-executor report --matrix reports/matrix/trace_matrix.yaml --runs runs --kind traceability --format markdown --test-cases plans --generated-at 2026-11-01T12:00:00Z -o reports/traceability.md
    Note over Report: S6 reads: reports/matrix/, plans/, runs/ writes: reports/

    %% vv-arrow A7
    Matrix ->> Report: render traceability report (AsciiDoc)
    Note over Matrix,Report: A7 example: test-executor report --matrix reports/matrix/trace_matrix.yaml --runs runs --kind traceability --format asciidoc --test-cases plans --generated-at 2026-11-01T12:00:00Z -o reports/traceability.adoc

    Tester ->> Bash: Execute test case <br>input: Test Case Shell Script
    %% replaced single execution step with alternative paths
    alt Manual Execution (includes manual steps)
        Tester ->> Bash: manual steps + automatic steps
    else Automatic Execution (without manual steps)
        Tester ->> Bash: only automatic steps
    end

    Bash ->> DUT: run test commands (manual/automated)
    DUT -->> Bash: output data

    Note over Bash,Tester: Artifact: <br>1. Test Execution Log (.json), PK={id,timestamp} <br> 2. 'Actual Output' Output files (actual.log), PK={id,timestamp}

    Tester ->> Verifier: Verify Test Execution<br>input: Test Case Execution Log, Test Case YAML
    Verifier ->> Verifier: verify expectations
    Note over Verifier,Tester: Artifact: <br>1. Test Verification Log (.json) PK={id,timestamp} <br> 2. Test Execution Result (.xml) PK={id,version,timestamp}

    Tester ->> Reports: Generate Test Plan Documentation (input: set of (Test Execution Result [.xml] + Test Case YAML [.yaml]))
    Note over Reports,Tester: Artifact: Test Plan Documentation (.adoc/.html/.pdf)<br>PK={id,version,timestamp}
